@startuml Mistral + DBaaS: provisioning, restore, credential ownership

actor "User" as user
participant "Cloud Backuper" as CB
participant "Mistral Operator" as MO
participant "Update DB Job" as MUJ
participant "DBaaS Aggregator" as DBaaS
database "Postgres" as P

entity "Mistral CM" as MCM
entity "Mistral Secret" as MS
collections "Mistral Services" as MSVC

note across
  Mistral integrated with DBaaS (mistralCommonParams.dbaas.integrationEnabled=true):
  - DBaaS is the SOURCE OF TRUTH for DB connection + credentials.
  - Secret + CM are a read cache. Operator is PULL-ONLY
  - Credentials are NEVER changed by editing the Secret; they change in DBaaS
    (restore / rotate-password) and the operator propagates them.
  - DB creation strategy is auto-routed by get-by-classifier so that
    greenfield, legacy-manual (brownfield) and restore all share one code path.
  - GUARDRAIL: never native-create a DB on top of an existing physical DB with data.
end note

== Deploy / Reconcile (on.create, on.update) ==

group sync_db_connection_from_dbaas()

    MO -> DBaaS: POST get-by-classifier/postgresql\n{ classifier, userRole }

    alt DB found, internal (DBaaS-managed)
        DBaaS --> MO: connectionProperties\n(host, port, authDbName, username, password)
        note right of MO
          Covers greenfield-after-create
          AND brownfield-after-migrate.
        end note

    else DB found, external / not migrated (brownfield in transition)
        DBaaS --> MO: connection (external)
        MO -> DBaaS: Migrate external -> internal\n(keep credentials)
        MO -> DBaaS: get-by-classifier
        DBaaS --> MO: connectionProperties

    else DB not found in DBaaS
        MO -> P: Probe: does physical DB exist with data?\n(using current Secret creds)
        alt Legacy manual DB exists with data
            note right of MO: GUARDRAIL -> adopt, do NOT create
            MO -> DBaaS: Register External DB\n(registration/externally_manageable)
            MO -> DBaaS: Migrate external -> internal\n(keep credentials)
            MO -> DBaaS: get-by-classifier
            DBaaS --> MO: connectionProperties
        else True greenfield (no DB anywhere)
            MO -> DBaaS: PUT databases (get-or-create,\ndbOwner=mistral)
            DBaaS -> P: Create DB + user
            DBaaS --> MO: connectionProperties
        end
    end

    MO -> MS: Read current pg-user / pg-password
    MO -> MCM: Read current pg-host / pg-port / pg-db-name
    MO -> MO: compare DBaaS connection with CM + Secret

    alt Drift (restore / rotation / first sync)
        MO -> MSVC: Scale down services
        MO -> MCM: Patch pg-host / pg-port / pg-db-name
        MO -> MS: Patch pg-user / pg-password
        MO -> MUJ: Run Update DB Job (dbaas mode)
        MUJ -> P: upgrade head + populate\n(no create_db / create_user)
        MO -> MSVC: Scale up services
    else No drift
        MO -> MUJ: Run Update DB Job (dbaas mode)
        MUJ -> P: upgrade head + populate
        MO -> MSVC: Deploy / ensure services
    end
end

MSVC -> MS: Read pg-user / pg-password (envs.sh)
MSVC -> MCM: Read pg-host / pg-port / pg-db-name
MSVC -> P: Connect



@enduml
